## Quick Code Demo (What You'd See in DevTools)

**Layout thrashing demo:**
```js
// BAD version — forces layout recalculation 200 times
elements.forEach(el => {
  el.style.width = '20px';  // WRITE
  void el.offsetHeight;     // READ — forces synchronous layout, every time
});

// GOOD version — forces layout recalculation ~once
const heights = elements.map(el => el.offsetHeight); // all reads first
elements.forEach((el, i) => {
  el.style.width = (heights[i] + 10) + 'px'; // all writes after
});
```
If you record this in Chrome DevTools' **Performance** tab, the BAD version shows a dense wall of purple "Layout" bars — one per element. The GOOD version shows just one or two.

**Animation comparison:**
```js
// Expensive — Layout + Paint + Composite, every single frame
el.style.left = distance + 'px';

// Cheap — Composite only
el.style.transform = `translateX(${distance}px)`;
```

